       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses far above that raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Overdose can also cause shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and these effects can last a long time because the drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, if you want a lower starting dose\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason. I can then enter it with a note saying you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
