       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but 50 mg of amlodipine is in the range where overdoses have caused refractory hypotension, shock, and pulmonary edema. No indication I know of calls for a single daily dose that high, and the 10 mg maximum is well established. A once-daily dose of 50 mg would also build up over several days because of the drug's long half-life.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily.** I can do this now, with a note that you want to titrate or add a second agent for blood pressure control.\n- **Add another agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, a different class could help, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. I can enter that order if you tell me which one.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** If you have an unusual reason for this dose, a pharmacist or clinical pharmacology consult can review it with you. You could then place the order directly with their sign-off.\n\nTell me which you'd like. If you meant a different dose or drug, give me the details and I'll enter it."
